[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mInline per-field messages[39m
     [38;5;246mEach invalid field gets its message rendered next to it in the DOM, cleared on the next submit. The reusable layer
[39m     [38;5;246mowns rendering, so every form gets consistent error UI for free.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Keep console-only for now
     [38;5;246mThe reusable layer returns structured errors; displaying them stays each form's problem. Smallest scope, but every
[39m     [38;5;246mnew form re-solves error UI.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m One summary block per form
     [38;5;246mA single error region at the top of the form lists all failures. Simpler DOM contract than per-field, less precise
[39m     [38;5;246mfor the user.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m Inline messages + disabled submit
     [38;5;246mPer-field messages plus live validation on blur/input that keeps the submit button disabled until the form is [39m
     [38;5;246mvalid. Largest scope: adds an event/state layer beyond submit-time checking.[39m
